<title>UK: Whitbread set to buy Pizzaland - paper.</title>
<headline>Whitbread set to buy Pizzaland - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewer and leisure group Whitbread Plc is poised to buy restaurant chain owner Brightreasons, owner of the Pizzaland, Bella Pasta and Pizza Piazza chains, for around 90 million stg, the Guardian newspaper reported.</p>
<p>In its Wednesday edition, the Guardian said Whitbread has been in talks for several weeks to buy the privately-owned 180 restaurant group and has outbid restaurant chain City Centre, which owns the Deep Pan Pizza and Garfunkels chains.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
